"ποι-ητής, οῦ, ὁ, maker, μηχανημάτων Id. Cyr. 1.6.38 ; κλίνης Pl. R. 597d ; τὸν π. καὶ πατέρα τοῦδε τοῦ παντός Id. Ti. 28c ; ζῴων, of the painter, Id. Sph. 234a ; inventor, θεῶν Id. Euthphr. 3b ; νόμων lawgiver, Id. Def. 415b . workman, PSI 4.388.8 , al. (iii B.C., pl.). composer of a poem, author, π. κωμῳδίας Pl. Lg. 935e ; π. καινῶν δραμάτων, τραγῳδιῶν κτλ. SIG 1079.2 , al. ( Magn. Mae., ii/i B.C.): abs., poet, Hdt. 2.53 , Ar. Ra. 96 , 1030 , Pl. Ion 534b , etc.; Homer was called ὁ π., Pl. Grg. 485d , Arist. Rh. 1365a11 , 1380b28 , Teles p.34 H., Plb. 12.21.3 , Str. 1.1.10 , A.D. Synt. 26.19 , etc.; so also Hesiod, Pl. Lg. 901a ; and others, Id. Thg. 125e , D.Chr. 78.44 . composer of music, Pl. Lg. 812d . author of a speech, opp. deliverer of it, π. λόγων Id. Euthd. 305b , cf. Phdr. 234e , 278e , Alcid. Soph. 34 , Isoc. 15.192 . (Written ποητής IG 22.2319.65 , SIG 711 L 35 (Delph., ii B.C.), etc.)"